alignedBlock is operation
alignedBlock purpose "A zeroed block of a size whose address is a multiple of a power of two; the address 0 when there is none. Alignments the runtime's heap gives anyway (16 bytes, 32 on Linux) take a plain block. On Linux a larger one is cut from a block of its own with the header a small block has, so free puts it back on the free list of its size (a large one's munmap fails and its mapping is left); on Windows HeapAlloc cannot align, so blocks are taken together until one is aligned and the others given back"
